# System-wide authorized keys for root (see sshd_config: AuthorizedKeysFile).
#
# Kept here rather than in /root/.ssh because the overlay is applied with
# `rsync --chmod=u=rwX,go=rX`, which would rewrite /root from 0700 to 0755 as a
# side effect. sshd's StrictModes only rejects keys that are group/world
# WRITABLE, so the 0644 this file lands with is fine.
#
# sshd_config lists .ssh/authorized_keys first, so an operator can still add a
# key to /root/.ssh on a live unit without rebuilding.
#
# Root login is key-only (PermitRootLogin prohibit-password). Emptying this
# file without providing another key locks SSH out entirely - and on the Pico
# Max there is no usable serial console, so the ONLY way back in would be a
# full reflash over USB. Treat this file as lockout-critical.
#
# Two keys are authorized, both Joral build hosts. A second key is not a
# weakening -- root login is key-only either way -- it removes a single point
# of lockout. That is not hypothetical: on 2026-09-11 a flashed image
# authorized only the first key, which the build host does not hold the
# private half of, and SSH fell through to a password prompt that
# prohibit-password can never satisfy.
